{title: 596 - Look for the Waymarks}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #596 • LOOK FOR THE WAYMARKS • 10s}
{lyricist: F. E. Belden}
{composer: F. E. Belden}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 596}
{meta: tune LOOK FOR THE WAYMARKS}
{meta: meter 10s}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Look for the way-marks as you journey [D7]on,
[G]Look for the way-marks passing one by one;
[G]Down through the ages, past the kingdoms four—
[G]Where are [Em]we standing? Look the way-marks o’er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Look for the way-marks, the [G/D]great prophetic way-marks,
[Am]Down through the ages, past the kingdoms four.
[G]Look for the waymarks, [C]the great prophetic [Am]way-marks;
[Am]The journey's almost o'er.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]First, the Assyrian kingdom ruled [D7]the world,
[G]Then Medo-Persia's banners were unfurled;
[G]And after Greece held universal sway,
[G]Rome seized [Em]the scepter'where are we today?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Down in the feet of iron and [D7]of clay,
[G]Weak and divided, soon to pass away;
[G]What will the next great, glorious drama be?
[G]Christ and [Em]His coming, and eternity.
{end_of_verse}
